1. Introduction
The contamination of water supplies by traces of heavy metals is a
global issue causing serious environmental and health concerns and, as a
consequence, an increasing of demand for water remediation technologies
[1-3].
Cadmium (Cd) is widely distributed throughout the Earth’s crust,
particularly abundant in zinc and lead ores, and is presented in anthropogenic

* Corresponding authors: ibtissemounifi@yahoo.com (I. Ounifi); a.figoli@itm.cnr.it (A. Figoli)
DOI:http://www.msrjournal.com/article_38302.html
