2.4. Scanning electron microscopy (SEM)
The morphology of CA membranes was analysed using a scanning
electron microscope (Zeiss EVO MA 100, Assing, Italy). In order to observe
the membrane cross sections, membranes were first frozen in liquid nitrogen
and then submitted to fracture. All samples (cross sections top and bottom
surfaces) were sputter-coated with a thin gold film prior to SEM observation.
2.5. Contact angle
The hydrophilic/hydrophobic nature of the membranes was evaluated
byan optical camera using an Attension Theta T200 blood pressure monitor
(Biolin Scientific, Sweeden). The software used was "One Attension
Software". The measurements were performed using ultrapure water drop
(5µL). For all membranes, at least 3 measurements were taken and the
average value and the corresponding standard deviation were then calculated.

